ixing and that it was an  internal matter for tsm so tsm wasn't  adding anything to their statement for  now and peter zhang was not elaborating  on the details of his dismissal however  on sunday dexato's richard lewis  published an article in which he stated  that sources informed them peter zhang  had been dismissed because of an  agent-style setup where he'd secured  chinese and taiwanese players a spot on  tsm for a cut of their earnings these  sources told dexerto that peter zhang  would take a portion of the player's  earnings usually much higher than a  standard agent's fee and then ensured  that they had a spot on the team if this  was the case it would naturally be a big  conflict of interest to act as both  agent and coach sources also told  dexerto that peter zhang had been  borrowing quote significant sums of  money from many figures under the tsm  organization including players from both  the main and academy roster and that  quote when affected parties raised  concerns about the loans they started to  be paid back at the time of reporting  this almost all the money has been  recouped peter zhang confirmed the  existence of these loans to dexerto and  told them he needed the money for a  family emergency for which he showed  proof of him requesting time off for  this as for the coach agent role he said  the accusations of him playing both  coach and agent were either a  misunderstanding or a malicious framing  of events he cited one example with  tsm's academy support yersen and  admitted that while he did receive a one  thousand dollar a month cut from his  paycheck that money was always sent  directly to the player's agent he  explained that this was because as a us  green card holder he had bank accounts  in both countries and so was able to  facilitate these transactions more  easily now between tsm's announcement  and dexato's article doublelift had  alluded on stream that he knew some of  the details of this story doublelift  tsm's former ad carry has had clashes  with its own original which have led in  part to a recent riot investigation into  the ceo over alleged work misconduct and  bullying of employees doublelift knew  peter zhang from his time at tsm and  when the dexerto article came out he  added some more allegations to the pile  i do not want to say who he has 200k  from but what i will say is that he got  multiple players multiple players on tsm  to send him anywhere between 12 and 25k  and then that same day those players  before that wire transfer went through  those players canceled it and like saved  their money doublelift also alleged that  former tsm support sword art had asked  peter zhang to sell his car for him when  the taiwanese star returned home after a  year with the team at that point i was  like okay this guy he's doing a bunch of  sketchy under the table stuff he owes  this guy like a metric ton of money that  was a super expensive car i knew that he  definitely owed sword art money and i  was like this is  peter zhang told dexerto that he  recognizes his wrongdoing that he will  pay sword art back in full that the  other claims about him are not true and  that he will work with right in any  investigation they conduct to prove his  innocence doublelift also said that  peter zhang had recently asked him for  seventy thousand dollars to cover  medical expenses for his grandma who was  dying in hospital if somebody asked me  in an emergency for a few thousand  dollars or somebody that i really really  trusted i would lend them a pretty large  amount of money seventy thousand someone  i barely know no that's not happening  doublelift added that when he asked some  of their mutual friends he found they've  been asked and told similar things by  peter zhang clearly there's still a lot  that's unknown here there are questions  that only tsm peter zhang all the people  he allegedly asked for money from can  answer and if you've been watching any  of my recent videos on tsm you'll know 